Command sequence (Ruby 3.3.1, /tmp/sf-maturity-demo, fresh git repo with
Gemfile containing rails+rspec, lib/app.rb, spec/app_spec.rb):

  soft-foundry init --no-onboard
    -> maturity: scanned - level 0 (unknown), 1 gap(s) to the next level.
    -> .ai/repository.yml: technology.languages=[ruby], technology.frameworks=[rails],
       technology.testing=[ruby], infrastructure.detected_or_not_applicable=NOT_APPLICABLE
       (no IaC found), repository.execution_path_known=UNKNOWN (fewer than two signals:
       Gemfile-only repo has no README/Rakefile/CI in this minimal fixture)
    -> maturity.gaps = [{level: 1, capability: repository.execution_path_known, status: UNKNOWN}]

  soft-foundry init --no-onboard   (second run)
    -> maturity: already assessed (unknown); skipping. Use --reassess to force.
    -> .ai/repository.yml unchanged

  soft-foundry init --no-onboard --reassess
    -> maturity: scanned - level 0 (unknown), 1 gap(s) to the next level.
    -> re-ran despite prior assessment, as requested
